## Main change

The finite cyclic carrier is no longer only an intrinsic mathematical object of the strict weighted kernel. Under explicit channel assumptions it now has a concrete, label-free operational signature.

### Markov/heat

The strict radial heat kernel preserves the complete shell order for every finite positive time:

`p0(t)>p1(t)>...>p6(t)`.

This follows from an exact irreducible Metzler evolution for the six shell differences.

Conditioning on a recorded exit removes the overall clock scale exactly:

`P(next=j | leave i)=W_ij/s_i`.

Thus the two dominant destinations from each state recover the intrinsic nearest-neighbor graph without a supplied cyclic labeling.

### Reversible calculi

Unitary and wave records recover the same nearest shell in explicit conservative short-time windows. Unlike heat, they also exhibit certified later shell crossings in the supplied finite model. Hence shell ordering can serve as an ordinal dynamics discriminator once a physical control/time map exists.

### Falsifiability

A same-symmetry/same-equilibrium/same-exit-rate control with shell 1 and shell 2 swapped predicts a different carrier and is strongly distinguishable from clock-free destination records. Therefore the operational bridge is not a restatement of D12 symmetry or equilibrium.

